  "description": "WIGYEQ crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C110 H162 Eu8 O26,2(C7 H8). From the CIF bond table, Eu1 (Eu) has 7 O neighbors; Eu2 (Eu) has 7 O neighbors; Eu3 (Eu) has 7 O neighbors; Eu4 (Eu) has 7 O neighbors; Eu1B (Eu) has 7 O neighbors; Eu2B (Eu) has 7 O neighbors; Eu4B (Eu) has 7 O neighbors; Eu3B (Eu) has 7 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 24 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.603-5.347 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 86.12-167.57°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula H10[Eu8O8(OC6H3Me2-2,6)10(OiPr)2(THF)6]. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 OiPr (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
